{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>You open</b> — And the word ואתה in the verse above serves here too, and thus it is ואתה פותח את ידך, and thus: כי אלהי אבי בעזרי." "<b>desire</b> — that which suffices for them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {0 "The verse 'above' (i.e., the preceding verse, 145:15) also begins with ואתה; the reference to כי אלהי אבי בעזרי is uncertain — it does not match any standard biblical verse and may be corrupt or a partial quotation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:52.319049437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}